{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 3 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`: `validity()`, `impact_plan()`, `pass3_decide`, `pass3_over_findings`) is deterministic and every input it needs is in the v2 sidecar (`sidecar.py:702-703` persists per-finding `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` losslessly). `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` and `docs/experiments/calibrate_plan_review_thresholds.py` prove the replay works but are one-off scripts with hardcoded baselines.\n\n`orchestrator.pass3_over_findings(findings, verifs, *, execution_review=False)` (`orchestrator.py:662-711`) is the REAL LIVE plan-review path: `_threshold_for` special-cases `\"prerequisite-consistency\" -> (0.60, True)`, else resolves live via `_criteria.threshold_for(criteria, crit_by_id, gate=\"plan_review\")` (`crit_by_id = registry.by_id()`), bumps `block_threshold = max(bt, 0.80)` when `execution_review and blocking_enabled`; applies `_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded` (neutralizes on-target veto to `\"na\"` for findings whose criteria don't intersect `registry.CODEBASE_GROUNDED`) before `review_kernel.pass3_over_findings(..., threshold_for=_threshold_for, impact_fn=review_kernel.impact_plan, execution_review=...)`.\n\n**Registry drift is a distinct axis from `impact_model_version`.** Thresholds live in `criteria_routing.json`, governed by `regver` — not `impact_model_version`. Comparing \"live-resolved thresholds\" against a \"stored decision\" flips whenever `regver` moved since the review ran, even with `impact_model_version` unchanged. Tier-0 computes THREE things per finding:\n\n1. **stored** — the decision persisted in the sidecar.\n2. **replayed-stored** — `review_kernel.pass3_decide` fed the finding's PERSISTED `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` (no re-resolution) — pure harness self-check; MUST always equal `stored`, independent of registry drift.\n3. **live-baseline** — `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` (current production, live-resolved thresholds) — may legitimately differ from `stored` when `regver` drifted (\"registry drift\", not a flip).\n\n**Candidate** (`--candidate <name>`) is diffed against **live-baseline** — Tier-0's actual purpose. Resolved via `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/candidates/__init__.py`'s `CANDIDATES: dict[str, Candidate]` (`Candidate`: `overlay: dict[str, tuple[float, bool]]` per-criterion threshold/posture override, `impact_fn: Callable = review_kernel.impact_plan`). `\"current\"` is built-in with an empty overlay and default `impact_fn`. The candidate's `threshold_for` mirrors `_threshold_for`'s logic resolved against the overlay; `_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded` applied identically; then `review_kernel.pass3_over_findings(..., threshold_for=<mirrored>, impact_fn=<candidate's>, execution_review=...)`.\n\n`corpus.build_corpus`'s cache rows are summary-only. `findings`/`verification` need the SAME re-read `labels.py` uses: `corpus._enumerate_event_blobs` + `_batch_cat` matched by `review_event_uuid`, then `data[\"findings\"]`.\n\n**Plan-v4->v5 baseline, made importable.** `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py:162` `legacy_impact_plan(attrs)`: shipped `decide.impact_plan` scores pre-v5 ordinal grades (`low|medium|high`) as 0.0, collapsing the baseline — the script pins `legacy_impact_plan` (line 272) as the PRE-v5 baseline. `docs/calibration/` has NO `__init__.py` and is not on the import path, so `legacy_impact_plan`/`classify`/`RULES` (lines 124-162) are relocated verbatim into a NEW importable module `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py`; `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` is updated to `import` them from there (no duplication, script behavior unchanged). AC2's replay imports from the new module, pairing `classify`/`RULES` (grade->kind mapping) with `legacy_impact_plan` as the OLD-side impact function for that one comparison; every other comparison uses `review_kernel.impact_plan`.\n\nTicket-level labels (`labels.py`, closed) need `show_ticket` per ticket — too slow at full-corpus scale. Label-proxy metrics are SEPARATE, OPTIONAL: only over a supplied `labels-<hash>.jsonl`, report states coverage fraction.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (+ `legacy_v4_baseline.py`, `candidates/__init__.py`, `report.py`, `__main__.py`):\n\n- Extract `classify`/`RULES`/`legacy_impact_plan` from `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` into `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py`; update the doc script to import them from there.\n- Input: corpus (`corpus.build_corpus`), OPTIONAL `labels_path`, `--candidate <name>` resolved through `candidates.CANDIDATES[name]` (`KeyError` -> clear error listing known names).\n- Full-body re-read per row via `_enumerate_event_blobs`/`_batch_cat`; `data[\"findings\"]` + per-index persisted thresholds + `verification` feed Pass-3.\n- `__main__.py`: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate <name> [--labels <path>]`.\n- Per finding compute `stored`, `replayed-stored` (persisted thresholds, `pass3_decide` only — assert-equal to `stored` in tests, not reported as a \"flip\"), `live-baseline` (`orchestrator.pass3_over_findings`), `candidate` (mirrored resolver + overlay/impact_fn).\n- Plan-v4->v5 replay (AC2): `legacy_v4_baseline.classify`/`RULES` grade->kind mapping, compared against `legacy_v4_baseline.legacy_impact_plan` as the pre-v5 baseline for that comparison only.\n- Report (`tier0-<candidate-name>-<date>.md` + JSON): flip matrix segmented as (a) `stored` vs `live-baseline` = registry-drift count, (b) `live-baseline` vs `candidate` = candidate-induced flips (primary signal), friction rate, per-criterion deltas, priority distribution shift. IF `labels_path` supplied: label-proxy metrics with coverage fraction. ELSE states not computed.\n- Post-verdict floors replayed only when inputs present in the sidecar; otherwise reported as not replayed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py` (new — relocated from `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py`)\n- `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` (edited — imports from the new module instead of defining locally)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/candidates/__init__.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/report.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier0-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: `replayed-stored` (persisted thresholds) exactly equals `stored` for every fixture finding; a fixture with a registry threshold DIFFERENT from its persisted `block_threshold` shows `live-baseline` != `stored` (registry drift) while `replayed-stored` still == `stored`; candidate `\"current\"` == `live-baseline` for every finding; an overlay lowering one criterion's threshold flips exactly the findings between old/new thresholds; `prerequisite-consistency` special case and `execution_review` bump each exercised once; unknown `--candidate` name raises a clear error; v1 sidecar lacking `block_threshold` skipped and counted; pre-v5 graded row classified via `legacy_v4_baseline.classify` and compared against `legacy_v4_baseline.legacy_impact_plan`; `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` still runs after the extraction (its own script-level check); label-proxy metrics omitted without `labels_path`; `__main__.py`'s `tier0` subcommand dispatches correctly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current` over the real corpus reports zero `replayed-stored` vs `stored` mismatches (harness self-check) for every finding; checked by the generated report.\n- [ ] Replaying the plan-v4->plan-v5 change (via the relocated `legacy_v4_baseline.classify`/`RULES`/`legacy_impact_plan`) reproduces its documented direction and approximate magnitude; checked against `docs/calibration/`.\n- [ ] The report separately states registry-drift flips (`stored` vs `live-baseline`) and candidate-induced flips (`live-baseline` vs `candidate`), plus friction rate and per-criterion deltas; checked by inspection of one report.\n- [ ] IF a labels file is supplied, the report additionally contains label-proxy metrics with coverage fraction, annotated against the noise band; checked by inspection when available.\n- [ ] The Pass-3 replay itself (excluding any optional label-proxy step) completes in under 5 minutes on a laptop over the real corpus, with zero LLM calls; checked by timing and no provider credentials.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788086973012947745,"uuid":"7c06cac0-7d8d-44de-b0c3-12ede3629cf0"}